SUMMARY:The Morganton Greenway Is Back! Let's Walk It!
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nWe will be joining the As
 heville Amblers Walking Club for their walks on the Morganton Greenway. Th
 ese are free walks\, although the Amblers accept donations ($4 suggested).
  There may also be walkers from other groups there\, including AARP\, Stry
 der\, and more.\n\nChoose between 5 KM/3.1 miles and 10 KM/6.2 miles guide
 d walks. The walks will start in the parking lot at the end of Greenlee Fo
 rd Rd. We will meet at 8:30 for registration with step off at 9:00.\n\nThi
 s is a pleasant walk along the Catawba River with its rapids\, smooth flow
 ing areas\, grassy areas with Frisbee Golf Course\, and shaded walkways. I
 t also goes out to Freedom High School. The course is flat and paved. You 
 may want to bring some peanuts with you as the squirrels are *very* friend
 ly.\n\nDress for the weather\; consider a hat and sunscreen. Tennis shoes 
 should be fine. I will take a walking stick just in case\, but don't expec
 t to use it. Dogs are welcome. Strollers should be fine. As always\, bring
  plenty of water and a protein snack.\n\nIt is likely a group of walkers w
 ill go to lunch together\, perhaps at Boulevard BBQ. Feel free to join the
  meal.
