SUMMARY:Walk the Ethnobotany Trail and More at the NC Arboretum
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nMeet inside the Baker Vis
 itor Center which opens at 9:00 a.m. Restrooms are available at the start 
 point. We will start walking as soon as everyone has arrived\, hopefully n
 o later than 9:05.\n\nThe walk is a guided 5 KM trail. There are some mode
 rate hills and stair climbing. A significant part of the route is on well-
 groomed trails with very few obstacles. Some people will want walking pole
 s.\n\nWe will walk down Running Cedar Road to Bent Creak Road. Going down 
 Bent Creek Road\, we will turn onto the Ethnobotany Trail\, and then back 
 onto Bent Creek Road. We will go back up Wesley Branch Trail to the Willow
  Pond and thence back to the start point.\n\nDress for the weather\; consi
 der a hat and sunscreen. Sneakers should be fine\, unless it has rained re
 cently. Be sure to bring **plenty of water** and a protein snack.\n\nDogs 
 on leash are welcome but are not allowed in buildings or in the Bonsai Exh
 ibit. Trail strollers should be ok.\n\nThe NC Arboretum does not have an a
 dmission fee\, but they charge $25 per car parking fee (so pack as many pe
 ople in your car as you can). We recommend the driver purchase the lowest 
 level annual membership which includes free parking. (Of course\, you may 
 want a higher-level membership\, your choice.) We walk at the Arboretum at
  least six times per year.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/315003613/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260528T233934Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260528T233934Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
