SUMMARY:On National Read a Book Day\, Let's Walk at Lake Junaluska
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nSeptember 6 is National R
 ead a Book Day. Right before we step-off\, let's share with each other the
  title of a book we recommend the others read too. If you are able to "sho
 w and tell" bring the book with you\, so much the better. Don't worry\, we
 'll give you time to put the book back in your car before we step-off on t
 he walk. (I don't want to carry a book on a 7 KM walk with hills!)\n\nGath
 er at 2:00 at Lake Junaluska inside the Bethea Welcome Center. This will b
 e a 7 KM/4 mile route. The walk does not just go around the lake\, but up 
 to Lambuth Inn\, along the Rose Walk\, and through the Nature Garden. The 
 view from Inspiration Point is a must-see!\n\nDress for the weather. Consi
 der a hat and sunscreen. Some people may want walking poles\, especially f
 or the walk up to Lambuth Inn\; tennis shoes should be fine. It is particu
 larly important that walkers bring a protein snack and **plenty of** **wat
 er**. Restrooms are available at the Welcome Center\, at Lambuth Inn\, and
  along the route. Dogs on leash are welcome. Strollers are ok.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/315475899/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260629T211358Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260629T211358Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
