SUMMARY:Let's Walk: It's Leaf Season at the NC Arboretum
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nMeet inside the Baker Vis
 itor Center. Restrooms are available at the start point. We will start wal
 king as soon as everyone has arrived.\n\nThe walk is a guided 5 KM trail. 
 There are some moderate hills and stair climbing. A significant part of th
 e route is on well-groomed trails with very few obstacles. Some people wil
 l want walking poles.\n\nWe will walk down Wesley Branch Trail to Bent Cre
 ek Road. Traveling down Bent Creek Road\, we will loop through the Azalea 
 Garden a little further than we usually go. The Azaleas won't be in bloom\
 , but it will be leaf season after all. We will continue down Bent Creek R
 oad\, returning to the parking lot via Wolf Branch Road and Greenhouse Way
 . Before we quit\, we will walk through the Bonsai Exhibition Garden and t
 he Formal Gardens.\n\nDress for the weather\; consider a hat and sunscreen
 . Sneakers should be fine\, unless it has rained recently. Be sure to brin
 g **plenty of water** and a protein snack.\n\nDogs on leash are welcome bu
 t are not allowed in buildings or in the Bonsai Exhibit. Trail strollers s
 hould be ok.\n\nThe NC Arboretum does not have an admission fee\, but they
  charge $25 per car parking fee (so pack as many people in your car as you
  can). We recommend the driver purchase the lowest level annual membership
  which includes free parking. (Of course\, you may want a higher-level mem
 bership\, your choice.) We walk at the Arboretum at least six times per ye
 ar.
